join Narrator rightmost
Narrator: Heavy fog coils as you crest the ridge. Below, Lumora drowns beneath a shroud of smoke and shadow. Torchlight sputters like dying stars, flickering against the gloom. Distant screeches pierce the air—sharp, panicked—mingling with the anguished cries of villagers caught in fierce combat.
Narrator: From the silence erupts a scatter of footsteps and a blur of marmalade fur. Timot bursts onto the path, cloak lashing behind him, Brimble—his feline companion—clutched protectively in one arm. Far off, steel clashes ring through the chaos, swallowed by the cacophony of panicked voices.
leave Narrator
join Timot leftmost
Timot: By Aurethiel's grace… you made it! Quickly—this way. There's no time to lose!
Timot: At dawn, they broke the city gate. Our defenders hold what ground they can, but the village chokes beneath the encroaching dark—heavy, black, pendulous. It rolls like smoke through the streets, smothering flame and song alike.
Timot: You know how to fight? Good—then you'll survive this. Listen\: Move with the left stick or WASD keys. Aim and fire with the right stick or left mouse button. On mobile, use the touch controls. Hit ESC to pause. Stay nimble—keep moving, or the horde will drown you before you can draw breath!
Timot: Defend the town and buy us time while the villagers flee to the safe zones. Fifty souls must reach the extraction points—every one of them counts. When you have coin, seek my shop in the northwest corner. I'll have what defenses I can spare.
Timot: The guards hold the gates… but only just. The village is under siege—creatures of the Moribund Order pour in from every direction. We must evacuate the townsfolk, but we can't do it alone. We need you to buy us time.
Timot: I shall open my shop to you in what time we have left—what potions and trinkets I have are yours in exchange for whatever coin you may gather. Use them wisely. Every second you hold the line gives another villager a chance to escape.
Timot: Stand fast. Hold them off. The fate of Lumora rests in your hands.
join Brimble rightmost
Brimble: Meow! (Brimble meows, sharp and emphatic.)
Timot: I know, Brimble—the bakery's gone. But Lumora needs blade and bravery now, not snacks! Hurry back to the safety of the store! (Brimble runs off towards the town)
leave Brimble
join Narrator rightmost
Narrator: The earth rumbles beneath your feet as a distant roar rips through the hills. The din of battle intensifies—the monsters are drawing close now.
leave Narrator
Timot: (softly, voice rough with memory)
Timot: Annadaeus sang of this day—when peace still lingered and we were fools enough not to listen. She *knew* this storm was coming. She saw it long before the rest of us dared to believe it could.
Timot: (He pauses, eyes distant, as the sound of battle grows louder)
Timot: If we can endure… if we can hold the line just a little longer… perhaps she'll sing again. Not of warning, but of triumph.
Timot: (A faint smile touches his lips, fragile but defiant)
Timot: Until then, we fight. For the villagers. For the light. For the song yet unsung.
join Narrator rightmost
Narrator: Timot grips your shoulder, his hand firm despite the tremor in his voice.
Timot: Go now. This is your moment, hero. (He locks eyes with you, fear flickering behind the steel of his gaze)
Timot: Lumora cannot fall—not while the light endures. And you… you are that light now.
Timot: (A distant roar echoes through the valley. The ground shakes. Timot doesn't flinch.)
Timot: Show them why monsters fear the light.
[end_timeline]
